# Citation metadata, read by GitHub ("Cite this repository") and by Zenodo,
# which archives each GitHub release and gives it a DOI.
#
# At each release, set version to the release tag and date-released to the day
# the tag is cut. The DOI is added once Zenodo has archived a release: a
# placeholder that looks like an identifier is worse than an absent one.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: Dilution Planner
abstract: >-
  A deterministic browser tool that plans the volumes to combine to reach a
  stated target concentration, or an ordered set of them, from a stated stock,
  including the single intermediate dilution a step needs when its transfer is
  too small to pipette. It requires the user to declare what the stated volume
  is the volume of, the route, the diluent and the minimum reliable transfer
  volume, and withholds any plan the bench could not execute, naming the bound
  that failed. It plans preparation; it does not verify what was prepared. No
  model and no inference is applied to any reported value, and no data entered
  by a user leaves the browser.
authors:
